@startuml nodemedic-arch
' NodeMedic — system architecture (as implemented for AFA 2026)
' Reflects Spec 001 controller + Spec 002 agent + Spec 003 on-call UI,
' all live on cf1z (Azure kubeadm). Same image / chart / runbook works
' on AWS EKS — only credentials change per install.
'
' smetana is PlantUML's built-in layout engine — no graphviz needed.
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam rectangleBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam packageBackgroundColor  #F5F8FF
skinparam packageBorderColor      #6B8AB8
skinparam noteBackgroundColor     #FFFBEA
skinparam noteBorderColor         #B59A3B

title NodeMedic — system architecture (detail view)\nSpec 001 controller · Spec 002 agent · Spec 003 on-call UI\n(deployed on cf1z; cloud-agnostic — EKS / Azure kubeadm)\n\n//Numbered edges trace the end-to-end flow: ① detect → ⑬ reclaim.//\n//For the 1000ft summary see nodemedic-arch-overview.puml.//

legend top left
=== End-to-end flow (read edges in this order) ===
**①** NPD plugin flips a NodeCondition + writes Event
**②** Controller's NodeWatcher sees the transition (debounced)
**③** Controller CREATEs NHD CR (phase=Pending)
**④** Controller POSTs /diagnose to agent (async 202)
**⑤** Agent loop: tool calls (Bash · NR MCP · SDK built-ins)
   **⑤a** Reasoning via nerd-completion gateway (Opus 4.7)
**⑥** Tools read from worker / NR (read-only credentials)
**⑦** emit_report → Status().Update (phase=Diagnosed)
**⑧** Controller's reconciler runs the confidence gate
**⑨** Gate-pass → cordon Node (idempotent)
**⑩** Block Kit Slack post (Applied / HumanInLoop / Critical)
   **⑩a** On-call engineer pages on Slack
**⑪** Engineer port-forwards + opens per-case page in UI
**⑫** Engineer clicks Uncordon / Drain / Clear-skipDeletion
   **⑫a** UI patches Node + appends ui-action-history annotation
**⑬** MLC reclaims VM on its next reconcile (existing primitive)
endlegend

' ============================================================
' DETECTION PLANE — runs on every target cluster
' ============================================================
package "Target cluster\n(cf1z · Azure kubeadm    |    test-* · EKS)" as cluster {

  node "Worker node N" as wn {
    component "node-problem-detector\nDaemonSet (privileged)\n  · check-containerd.sh   (30s)\n  · check-kubelet-healthz.sh (30s)\n  · §4.2 catalog plugins\n     (conntrack · fd · pid · inode\n      disk · dns · imds — Day 2)" as npd
  }

  database "kube-apiserver\nNode.status.conditions[]\nNodeHealthDiagnosisAI CRs\nEvents" as api

  ' ----------------------------------------------------------
  ' Spec 001 — controller
  ' ----------------------------------------------------------
  package "cf-monitoring namespace" as ns {

    component "NodeMedic Controller\n(Spec 001 · Go · controller-runtime)\n  · NodeWatcher (debounce 30s)\n  · NHDReconciler (phase machine)\n  · ConfidenceGate (≥0.7 · ≥2 sources)\n  · Cordon executor (nodes/patch only)\n  · Block Kit Slack notifier" as ctrl

    ' ----------------------------------------------------------
    ' Spec 002 — agent
    ' ----------------------------------------------------------
    component "NodeMedic Agent\n(Spec 002 · Python · FastAPI · Claude Agent SDK)\n  · POST /diagnose (async 202)\n  · per-case asyncio worker\n  · ClaudeSDKClient PER CASE (no cross-case state)\n  · permission_mode = bypassPermissions\n     (safety = read-only credentials)\n  · Pre/PostToolUse hooks → stdout JSONL\n  · emit_report terminal tool\n     (schema validate + Status().Update)" as agent

    ' ----------------------------------------------------------
    ' Spec 003 — on-call UI
    ' ----------------------------------------------------------
    component "On-Call UI\n(Spec 003 · Go stdlib net/http + html/template)\n  · GET /                 — 24h list view\n  · GET /cases/<nhd>      — per-case detail\n  · POST .../uncordon\n  · POST .../clear-skip-deletion\n  · POST .../drain        — SSE stream\n  · audit → ui-action-history annotation\n     (last-20 FIFO ring buffer)\n  · 4-rule ClusterRole, no delete" as ui
  }

  npd  --> api : **①** NodeCondition flips True\n+ Event written
  api  --> ctrl : **②** watch Node + Event\n  (predicate = watched conditions)
  ctrl --> api : **③** CREATE NHD CR\nphase=Pending
  ctrl --> agent : **④** POST /diagnose\n(Bearer token, async 202)
  agent --> api  : **⑦** Status().Update\nstatus.diagnosis = {...}\nphase=Diagnosed
  api  --> ctrl  : **⑧** watch NHD update\n→ confidence gate
  ctrl --> wn    : **⑨** spec.unschedulable=true\n(cordon, idempotent)\n— gate-pass only
  ui   --> api   : **⑪** list / get / patch\n(NHD + Node + Pods + eviction)
}

' ============================================================
' AGENT TOOL PLANE — read-only investigation surface
' ============================================================
package "Agent tool surface (READ-ONLY by credential design)" as tools {

  component "Bash tool\n(SDK built-in)\n  · kubectl (in-cluster SA)\n  · ssh (hackathon key)\n  · aws / az CLI\n  · /proc, dmesg, journalctl" as bashtool

  component "New Relic MCP server\n(public HTTP MCP)\n  · execute_nrql_query\n  · analyze_entity_logs\n  · analyze_golden_metrics\n  · list_change_events\n  · get_entity / lookup_entity" as nrmcp

  component "SDK built-ins\n(Read · Grep · WebFetch · ...)" as sdkbuiltins
}

agent --> bashtool      : **⑤** tool calls\n(multi-turn loop)
agent --> nrmcp         : **⑤** tool calls
agent --> sdkbuiltins   : **⑤** tool calls
bashtool --> wn         : **⑥** kubectl / ssh\n(read-only)
nrmcp --> [NR account 1\n(staging)] : **⑥** NRQL · logs · metrics

' ============================================================
' MODEL PROVIDER
' ============================================================
package "Model provider" as models {
  component "nerd-completion gateway\n(internal · ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL)\n  · claude-opus-4-7    (primary)\n  · claude-sonnet-4-6  (fallback)\n  · /readyz availability fallback chain" as nerd
}
agent --> nerd : **⑤a** Anthropic SDK over HTTPS\n(token from Vault)

' ============================================================
' HUMAN-IN-THE-LOOP PLANE
' ============================================================
package "Human surface" as humans {
  actor "On-call engineer" as eng
  component "Slack #cf-oncall-alerts\n(Block Kit · severity-coded)\n  🚨 Applied   ⚠️ HumanInLoop   ❌ Critical" as slack
}

ctrl --> slack : **⑩** Block Kit POST\n(applied / human-in-loop / critical)
slack --> eng  : **⑩a** page lands\n(View full diagnosis button)
eng --> ui : **⑪** kubectl port-forward\n+ click button →\nhttp://localhost:8080/\ncases/<nhd>
eng --> ui : **⑫** Uncordon · Drain ·\nClear-skipDeletion\n(modal-confirmed)

' ============================================================
' DOWNSTREAM REMEDIATION (existing platform primitive)
' ============================================================
component "MLC\n(machine-lifecycle-controller)\nreclaims VMs whose nodes\nare cordoned + skipDeletion=false" as mlc
ui  --> wn  : **⑫a** (via api)\nnode.spec.unschedulable=false\n— or — annotation\nmachine-lifecycle.newrelic.com/\nskipDeletion REMOVED
mlc --> wn  : **⑬** reconcile →\nVM reclaimed
api --> mlc : watch Nodes

' ============================================================
' Side notes
' ============================================================
note right of agent
  No agent-side termination ceiling
  (no max_turns, no cost cap,
   no wall-clock deadline).
  Spend bounded by API key budget;
  user-visible duration bounded by
  the controller's deadline (Spec 001 FR-5).
end note

note bottom of tools
  Hackathon-scope simplification
  (Constitution-bound):
  no can_use_tool allow-list;
  no SSH command prefix-match.
  Safety = least-privilege creds:
  IAM/RBAC/kube-SA/NR token are
  all READ-ONLY. Agent kube-SA
  explicitly lacks nodes/patch.
end note

note bottom of humans
  UI is anonymous behind
  kubectl port-forward
  (no SSO, no Ingress, no TLS).
  Action audit lives on the NHD CR's
  ui-action-history annotation
  (last-20 FIFO ring buffer)
  + structured stdout logs.
end note

note right of ctrl
  Confidence gate (binding):
   confidence ≥ 0.7
   ∧ |distinct evidence sources| ≥ 2
   ∧ recommendation ∈
       {Cordon, DrainAndCordon}
  Below threshold → HumanInLoop;
  no auto-cordon. UI still acts.
end note

@enduml
